WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:03.002
-You guys, former
President Donald Trump's

00:00:03.002 --> 00:00:04.871
second impeachment trial
began today.

00:00:04.871 --> 00:00:06.672
The House impeachment managers

00:00:06.672 --> 00:00:08.375
laid out powerful evidence
of his guilt,

00:00:08.375 --> 00:00:10.343
while most Republican
senators signaled

00:00:10.343 --> 00:00:12.411
that they have no interest
in holding him accountable.

00:00:12.411 --> 00:00:14.947
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:14.947 --> 00:00:19.418
♪♪

00:00:19.418 --> 00:00:21.888
The nation is currently facing
a series of calamities

00:00:21.888 --> 00:00:23.489 line:0%
unprecedented in our lifetime.

00:00:23.489 --> 00:00:25.825 line:0%
It's so bad that
Jake Tapper's brow furrows

00:00:25.825 --> 00:00:28.561 line:0%
have started encroaching
on the rest of his face.

00:00:28.561 --> 00:00:31.030 line:0%
He's starting to look like
a Shar Pei with gravitas.

00:00:31.030 --> 00:00:33.700 line:0%
And, in the short term,
things are only getting worse.

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:36.369 line:0%
Millions are unemployed and the
economy is still stalling,

00:00:36.369 --> 00:00:38.304 line:0%
the vaccine rollout
is still chaotic,

00:00:38.304 --> 00:00:41.674 line:0%
even as more contagious
COVID strains are spreading,

00:00:41.674 --> 00:00:43.676 line:0%
not to mention rising poverty
and child hunger,

00:00:43.676 --> 00:00:45.411 line:0%
while millions face
the threat of eviction

00:00:45.411 --> 00:00:46.912 line:0%
or losing
their health insurance.

00:00:46.912 --> 00:00:48.348
Oh, and also,
the former president

00:00:48.348 --> 00:00:49.882
is facing
a second impeachment trial

00:00:49.882 --> 00:00:51.350
for inciting
a violent insurrection

00:00:51.350 --> 00:00:52.385
that ransacked the Capitol

00:00:52.385 --> 00:00:53.620
and sought
to overthrow democracy.

00:00:53.620 --> 00:00:54.987
And I know I'm starting to sound

00:00:54.987 --> 00:00:57.290
like an African grey parrot
who was left alone

00:00:57.290 --> 00:00:59.158
with a collection
of Morrissey records,

00:00:59.158 --> 00:01:00.860
but this is where we are.

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:02.261
[ Squawk ]

00:01:02.261 --> 00:01:05.064
If you're a person with any
sort of platform right now,

00:01:05.064 --> 00:01:07.033
you could spend any amount
of time you want

00:01:07.033 --> 00:01:09.102
covering any of those topics.

00:01:09.102 --> 00:01:11.137
Or, if you're Fox News,

00:01:11.137 --> 00:01:13.572
you could spend precious
minutes, in prime time,

00:01:13.572 --> 00:01:15.775
covering whatever the [bleep]
this is.

00:01:15.775 --> 00:01:18.144 line:7%
-Jonathan Kay is a senior editor

00:01:18.144 --> 00:01:20.813 line:8%
at the online magazine
Quillette.

00:01:20.813 --> 00:01:23.783 line:14%
He did a throwaway tweet,

00:01:23.783 --> 00:01:26.453 line:15%
revealing that,
for the last three months,

00:01:26.453 --> 00:01:29.222 line:15%
he'd accidentally
been washing his hair

00:01:29.222 --> 00:01:31.056 line:14%
with his dog's shampoo.

00:01:31.056 --> 00:01:32.091 line:14%
And, next thing you know,

00:01:32.091 --> 00:01:34.327 line:8%
big-time Hollywood star
Seth Rogen

00:01:34.327 --> 00:01:37.263 line:8%
and small-time lefty hack
Keith Olbermann

00:01:37.263 --> 00:01:39.298 line:8%
and the rest of the
Blue Checkers

00:01:39.298 --> 00:01:41.233 line:7%
were pounding on him.

00:01:41.233 --> 00:01:43.069
-Yes, that's what Fox News

00:01:43.069 --> 00:01:45.637
was talking about last night --
dog shampoo.

00:01:45.637 --> 00:01:49.241
You know, the stuff Ted Cruz
uses to wash his beard.

00:01:49.241 --> 00:01:50.543
[ As Cruz ]
I also use Frontline.

00:01:50.543 --> 00:01:52.578
Got to keep those ticks away.

00:01:52.578 --> 00:01:54.313
I have no idea what this is
about and I have

00:01:54.313 --> 00:01:55.982
no interest in learning.
All I know is,

00:01:55.982 --> 00:01:59.084
the smaller the story
Fox News is focusing on,

00:01:59.084 --> 00:02:00.853
the bigger the story
they're ignoring is.

00:02:00.853 --> 00:02:02.221
If you ever tune in
to "Fox &amp; Friends"

00:02:02.221 --> 00:02:03.422
and they're talking about,
I don't know,

00:02:03.422 --> 00:02:04.624
whether vanilla ice cream

00:02:04.624 --> 00:02:06.325
is going to be canceled
for being too white,

00:02:06.325 --> 00:02:08.528 line:0%
just know the story on CNN
is probably...

00:02:10.763 --> 00:02:12.665
But that's what the GOP
is all about now --

00:02:12.665 --> 00:02:14.500
inane culture war bull[bleep]

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:16.535
There's not time
for insurrections or COVID

00:02:16.535 --> 00:02:18.570
when a poor man catches flak
for complaining

00:02:18.570 --> 00:02:21.007
the font that said "for Pets"
was too small to read,

00:02:21.007 --> 00:02:22.708
while ignoring that there was

00:02:22.708 --> 00:02:24.777
a picture of a dog
on the bottle.

00:02:24.777 --> 00:02:27.680
I lied. I did know what the
story was about. What can I say?

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:29.915
I follow big-time Hollywood star
Seth Rogen on Twitter.

00:02:29.915 --> 00:02:32.618
And if you're wondering
what incredibly cruel thing

00:02:32.618 --> 00:02:36.055
he said when he saw the "I've
been using dog shampoo" tweet,

00:02:36.055 --> 00:02:39.392
a tweet so cruel that Fox News
did a segment on it,

00:02:39.392 --> 00:02:40.460
it was this...

00:02:40.460 --> 00:02:41.761
[ Laughter ]

00:02:41.761 --> 00:02:43.762
I get it.
You see a tweet like that,

00:02:43.762 --> 00:02:45.598
the next thing you know,
you're stress-eating

00:02:45.598 --> 00:02:47.600
a box of human snacks.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:49.535
This isn't a political movement
with policy ideas.

00:02:49.535 --> 00:02:50.602
It's about culture.

00:02:50.602 --> 00:02:51.938
They want you to think antifa's

00:02:51.938 --> 00:02:53.706
coming to your house
with migrant caravans

00:02:53.706 --> 00:02:55.641
to take away your guns
and your dog

00:02:55.641 --> 00:02:57.610
and your human shampoo
with the picture of a dog on it.

00:02:57.610 --> 00:02:59.245
In fact, that's barely
an exaggeration.

00:02:59.245 --> 00:03:00.680
That's their actual
argument now --

00:03:00.680 --> 00:03:02.648
the Democrats
are just as responsible

00:03:02.648 --> 00:03:04.216
for inciting violence
as Trump is

00:03:04.216 --> 00:03:06.652
because Democrats
want immigration reform.

00:03:06.652 --> 00:03:10.689 line:15%
-Democrats are arguing
that Trump welcomed and incited

00:03:10.689 --> 00:03:14.159 line:15%
a violent incursion
into the Capitol.

00:03:14.159 --> 00:03:15.761 line:7%
When it is they

00:03:15.761 --> 00:03:17.563 line:7%
who are enticing illegals

00:03:17.563 --> 00:03:19.131 line:7%
to bust through our borders,

00:03:19.131 --> 00:03:20.867 line:7%
exploit our resources,

00:03:20.867 --> 00:03:22.268 line:7%
and commit crimes.

00:03:22.268 --> 00:03:23.736
-Exploit our resources?

00:03:23.736 --> 00:03:25.771
Do you think immigrants
are coming to America

00:03:25.771 --> 00:03:26.872
to open a copper mine?

00:03:26.872 --> 00:03:28.841
You sound like a desert warlord

00:03:28.841 --> 00:03:30.976
from the "Mad Max"
Cinematic Universe.

00:03:30.976 --> 00:03:34.046 line:0%
Who is your guest
for this segment...

00:03:34.046 --> 00:03:36.282 line:0%
Did you guys know his name
was the Doof Warrior?

00:03:36.282 --> 00:03:37.616
Yeah, I mean,
I know a lot of you did,

00:03:37.616 --> 00:03:39.452
but I bet the rest of you
just thought his name

00:03:39.452 --> 00:03:41.287
was something like
Flame-Throwing Guitar Guy.

00:03:41.287 --> 00:03:44.356
That's how kickass
"Mad Max" was, as a movie.

00:03:44.356 --> 00:03:47.593
They give him the dorkiest name
they could come up with

00:03:47.593 --> 00:03:49.328
and the movie still rocks.

00:03:49.328 --> 00:03:52.031
It's like, instead of Bane,
Tom Hardy's Batman villain

00:03:52.031 --> 00:03:54.067
had been called Dr. CPAP or...

00:03:57.003 --> 00:03:58.871
[ As Bane ]
Bad news, Batman.

00:03:58.871 --> 00:03:59.939
[ Laughter ]

00:03:59.939 --> 00:04:01.607
Schmagillicutty.

00:04:01.607 --> 00:04:02.975
[ Laughter ]

00:04:02.975 --> 00:04:06.145
Also, you used "busting
through our borders" already.

00:04:06.145 --> 00:04:08.447
You got Donald Trump elected
on those fish tales

00:04:08.447 --> 00:04:09.982
and I thought we made it
very clear

00:04:09.982 --> 00:04:12.317
that GOP platforms are like
stand-up comedy jokes --

00:04:12.317 --> 00:04:15.188
once you use one on TV,
you can never use it again.

00:04:15.188 --> 00:04:17.990
It's why prayer in schools,
explicit rap lyrics,

00:04:17.990 --> 00:04:19.358
and Murphy Brown's pregnancies

00:04:19.358 --> 00:04:21.728
were used in one election cycle
and then never again.

00:04:21.728 --> 00:04:23.963
You have four years
to come up with a new way

00:04:23.963 --> 00:04:25.330
to terrify
the people of Florida.

00:04:25.330 --> 00:04:28.067
Maybe claim the DNC
is trying to ban fan boats

00:04:28.067 --> 00:04:29.535
and jean shorts
that go to the ankle.

00:04:29.535 --> 00:04:30.669
What's that?

00:04:30.669 --> 00:04:32.304
The GOP's already doing that
and it will work

00:04:32.304 --> 00:04:34.540
and Lou Dobbs will suddenly be
our next president?

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:35.808
[ Laughing ]
Okay, man.

00:04:35.808 --> 00:04:38.010
Politics, you share are goofy.

00:04:38.010 --> 00:04:40.446
But, really, the truly
galling part is the idea

00:04:40.446 --> 00:04:43.148
that Democrats are somehow
enticing migrants to come here

00:04:43.148 --> 00:04:46.619
and "commit crimes" when Trump
is under investigation

00:04:46.619 --> 00:04:47.853
for, last I checked,
I don't know,

00:04:47.853 --> 00:04:49.655
30 different crimes?

00:04:49.655 --> 00:04:52.658
In fact, he's already confessed
to illegally using his charity

00:04:52.658 --> 00:04:54.560
as a personal checkbook
and he was

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:57.162
an unindicted co-conspirator
in the Michael Cohen case,

00:04:57.162 --> 00:04:59.398
you know, the one where
he secretly paid hush money

00:04:59.398 --> 00:05:00.733
during a presidential campaign

00:05:00.733 --> 00:05:02.467
to cover up an affair
with a porn star.

00:05:02.467 --> 00:05:04.971
Remember that episode?
That was way back in Season 1,

00:05:04.971 --> 00:05:07.073
when Trump still had Marcel.

00:05:07.073 --> 00:05:09.609
The Manhattan D.A.
and New York attorney general

00:05:09.609 --> 00:05:11.610
are both investigating Trump
and his businesses,

00:05:11.610 --> 00:05:13.011
the D.A. in Fulton County

00:05:13.011 --> 00:05:15.848
has been looking into whether
to open an investigation,

00:05:15.848 --> 00:05:18.217 line:0%
and, yesterday, the Georgia
secretary of state's office

00:05:18.217 --> 00:05:20.019 line:0%
said it opened
an official inquiry

00:05:20.019 --> 00:05:21.620
into Trump's
unhinged phone call,

00:05:21.620 --> 00:05:24.423
attempting to bully
Georgia election officials

00:05:24.423 --> 00:05:27.927
into throwing out legal ballots
and overturning the results.

00:05:27.927 --> 00:05:31.130
And I'm no lawyer, but it almost
certainly seems like a crime.

00:05:31.130 --> 00:05:33.800
One former federal prosecutor
told CNN it's...

00:05:50.149 --> 00:05:52.151
And even that is
a generous interpretation.

00:05:52.151 --> 00:05:53.586
Trump doesn't talk in code.

00:05:53.586 --> 00:05:56.823
He's like that idiot who calls
a weed dealer and uses code

00:05:56.823 --> 00:06:00.793
and then, uses the real word,
to make sure the code was right.

00:06:00.793 --> 00:06:01.860
"Hey, Scott, what's up?

00:06:01.860 --> 00:06:03.162
You got any, uh, tickets

00:06:03.162 --> 00:06:05.331
for the, uh, reggae concert?

00:06:05.331 --> 00:06:07.600
That's weed, right? Because
like the reggae guys like weed.

00:06:07.600 --> 00:06:09.802
Hello? Hello?"
[ Laughter ]

00:06:09.802 --> 00:06:11.837
In response,
Trump spokesman Jason Miller,

00:06:11.837 --> 00:06:13.905
the guy who looks like
he swapped heads

00:06:13.905 --> 00:06:15.240
with a Pez dispenser,

00:06:15.240 --> 00:06:18.343
said it was actually the fault
of Brad Raffensperger,

00:06:18.343 --> 00:06:19.478
the Georgia secretary of state,

00:06:19.478 --> 00:06:22.014
for taking the call,
in the first place.

00:06:33.425 --> 00:06:38.064
Man, where does Trump find these
fine purveyors of pretzel logic?

00:06:38.064 --> 00:06:41.300
"Look, Your Honor, if you don't
want my client stabbing people,

00:06:41.300 --> 00:06:43.268
then Cuisinart
shouldn't sell knives.

00:06:43.268 --> 00:06:44.503
Oh, oh, my bad.

00:06:44.503 --> 00:06:45.504
Wrong case.

00:06:45.504 --> 00:06:48.206
Uh, any chance Cuisinart
sells guns?

00:06:48.206 --> 00:06:49.942
Oh, I think you're --

00:06:49.942 --> 00:06:51.443
I think you're probably
going to jail.

00:06:51.443 --> 00:06:52.711
[ Laughter ]
It's not terrible.

00:06:52.711 --> 00:06:54.513
They have libraries."

00:06:54.513 --> 00:06:57.049
This guy is under investigation
for actual crimes,

00:06:57.049 --> 00:06:58.450
let alone
the impeachable offense

00:06:58.450 --> 00:07:00.652
of inciting an insurrection
against the U.S. Capitol.

00:07:00.652 --> 00:07:03.956
The least we can do is bar him
from ever holding office again.

00:07:03.956 --> 00:07:06.559
Instead, Republicans and their
allies in right-wing media

00:07:06.559 --> 00:07:08.160
are engaged
in a ridiculous attempt

00:07:08.160 --> 00:07:10.529
to equate Democrats
encouraging peaceful protests

00:07:10.529 --> 00:07:11.897
with Trump spending
several months

00:07:11.897 --> 00:07:14.733
feeding his unhinged base lies
about the election

00:07:14.733 --> 00:07:16.802
and fantasies
of violent retribution.

00:07:16.802 --> 00:07:18.404 line:8%
-I want to interview Chuck.
-[ Laughing ]

00:07:18.404 --> 00:07:20.006 line:7%
I want to interview Joe Biden.

00:07:20.006 --> 00:07:21.540 line:7%
I want to interview Kamala.

00:07:21.540 --> 00:07:23.075 line:8%
I want
to interview Pelosi.

00:07:23.075 --> 00:07:25.110 line:8%
I want to interview
Maxine Waters.

00:07:25.110 --> 00:07:27.312 line:8%
I want to interview Cory Booker,
Eric Holder.

00:07:27.312 --> 00:07:28.881 line:7%
I got a whole list.

00:07:28.881 --> 00:07:32.184 line:8%
Would you consider looking
at my list?

00:07:32.184 --> 00:07:33.252 line:7%
-[ Laughs ]

00:07:33.252 --> 00:07:34.720 line:8%
Yeah, I'll be glad
to look at it.

00:07:34.720 --> 00:07:37.623 line:8%
If the House managers want
to call one witness,

00:07:37.623 --> 00:07:40.259 line:8%
the defense is going to call
all the people you name,

00:07:40.259 --> 00:07:41.360 line:7%
and then some.

00:07:41.360 --> 00:07:42.761 line:0%
The impeachment in the House

00:07:42.761 --> 00:07:44.863 line:0%
took place without a hearing,

00:07:44.863 --> 00:07:46.765 line:0%
without one witness
being called,

00:07:46.765 --> 00:07:48.067 line:0%
and without a lawyer

00:07:48.067 --> 00:07:49.902 line:0%
for the president
of the United States.

00:07:49.902 --> 00:07:52.838 line:0%
You can't get a traffic ticket,
based on the procedures

00:07:52.838 --> 00:07:55.174 line:0%
they used to impeach
President Trump.

00:07:55.174 --> 00:07:57.409
-Okay, first of all, have you
ever gotten a traffic ticket?

00:07:57.409 --> 00:07:58.410
You can get one for anything.

00:07:58.410 --> 00:07:59.479
One time, I got in my car

00:07:59.479 --> 00:08:01.280
and found a $20 ticket
on the windshield

00:08:01.280 --> 00:08:04.116
for something called...

00:08:04.116 --> 00:08:06.585
In New York, we have something
called alternate side parking,

00:08:06.585 --> 00:08:09.088
which basically means
you get a traffic ticket,

00:08:09.088 --> 00:08:10.256
unless you can solve a riddle.

00:08:18.931 --> 00:08:20.532
Also, Sean,
congrats on your list.

00:08:20.532 --> 00:08:23.302
You sound like a toddler
talking to a mall Santa.

00:08:23.302 --> 00:08:24.470
[ As Hannity ]
We look at my list, please?

00:08:24.470 --> 00:08:26.772
I want a Tonka truck
and a Nerf gun

00:08:26.772 --> 00:08:28.240
and a regular-shaped head.

00:08:28.240 --> 00:08:29.708
[ Gravelly voice ]
Listen, kid,
I'm not really Santa,

00:08:29.708 --> 00:08:30.876
but I can tell you,

00:08:30.876 --> 00:08:32.911
you're probably stuck
with that head, bub.

00:08:32.911 --> 00:08:35.748
Now, most people aren't buying
these asinine arguments.

00:08:35.748 --> 00:08:38.884
A majority of Americans --
56% in a recent ABC News poll --

00:08:38.884 --> 00:08:41.687
want Trump convicted and barred
from ever holding office again,

00:08:41.687 --> 00:08:44.557
so cowardly Republicans are
hiding behind a new argument --

00:08:44.557 --> 00:08:48.127
impeaching a former president
is somehow unconstitutional.

00:08:48.127 --> 00:08:50.395 line:15%
-I want to read
this very revealing quote

00:08:50.395 --> 00:08:52.632 line:15%
from Senator James Lankford.
He says..

00:09:05.344 --> 00:09:06.678
-Oh, you're locked down?

00:09:06.678 --> 00:09:07.947
You're supposed to be the jury!

00:09:07.947 --> 00:09:10.616
Once again, these guys think
the standards that apply

00:09:10.616 --> 00:09:12.751
to everyone else
somehow doesn't apply to them.

00:09:12.751 --> 00:09:15.654
I mean, none of us could
get away with just announcing

00:09:15.654 --> 00:09:18.624
how we feel about a case
before the trial starts.

00:09:18.624 --> 00:09:21.160
I tried that one time
when I got called to jury duty.

00:09:21.160 --> 00:09:22.328
"I'm sorry, Your Honor, but,

00:09:22.328 --> 00:09:24.496
I feel strongly that,
if you burn yourself

00:09:24.496 --> 00:09:26.332
with hot McDonald's coffee,
you deserve it.

00:09:26.332 --> 00:09:29.034
I will never turn on Ronald!"

00:09:29.034 --> 00:09:30.803
The judge found me in contempt

00:09:30.803 --> 00:09:32.471
and sentenced me
to three months' house arrest

00:09:32.471 --> 00:09:35.474
with a painting
of a sea captain.

00:09:35.474 --> 00:09:37.209
That was on network television.

00:09:37.209 --> 00:09:38.777
[ Laughter ]

00:09:38.777 --> 00:09:41.213
Second, the idea that impeaching
a former president

00:09:41.213 --> 00:09:42.982
is unconstitutional
is ridiculous.

00:09:42.982 --> 00:09:44.784
It doesn't say that anywhere
in the Constitution.

00:09:44.784 --> 00:09:46.485
If you manage to flee
the scene of a crime

00:09:46.485 --> 00:09:47.687
before the cops can catch you,

00:09:47.687 --> 00:09:49.755
you don't get
to automatically go free.

00:09:49.755 --> 00:09:52.023
If that was the case, Trump
would've finished his speech

00:09:52.023 --> 00:09:54.326
and then immediately jumped
in a white Ford Bronco.

00:09:54.326 --> 00:09:56.895
And then, today, one of the
House impeachment managers,

00:09:56.895 --> 00:09:58.297
Congressman Jamie Raskin,

00:09:58.297 --> 00:10:00.666
made a powerful
and deeply emotional case

00:10:00.666 --> 00:10:02.868
and he argued in a convincing
and clear-cut way

00:10:02.868 --> 00:10:05.337
that this impeachment was,
in fact, constitutional,

00:10:05.337 --> 00:10:08.774
using both historical evidence
and also common sense.

00:10:08.774 --> 00:10:12.211 line:8%
-Their argument is that, if you
commit an impeachable offense

00:10:12.211 --> 00:10:14.146 line:8%
in your last few weeks
in office,

00:10:14.146 --> 00:10:18.250 line:8%
you do it with
constitutional impunity.

00:10:18.250 --> 00:10:21.220 line:7%
You get away with it.

00:10:21.220 --> 00:10:23.989 line:8%
In other words,
conduct that would be

00:10:23.989 --> 00:10:29.461 line:8%
a high crime and misdemeanor
in your first year as president

00:10:29.461 --> 00:10:32.130
and your second year
as president

00:10:32.130 --> 00:10:34.833
and your third
year as president

00:10:34.833 --> 00:10:35.867
and for the vast majority

00:10:35.867 --> 00:10:37.402
of your fourth year
as president,

00:10:37.402 --> 00:10:38.671
you can suddenly do

00:10:38.671 --> 00:10:41.573
in your last few weeks in office
without facing

00:10:41.573 --> 00:10:44.810
any constitutional
accountability at all.

00:10:44.810 --> 00:10:49.949
This would create
a brand-new January exception

00:10:49.949 --> 00:10:54.487
to the Constitution
of the United States of America.

00:10:54.487 --> 00:10:57.355
-Yeah, the founders didn't
intend to write in an exemption

00:10:57.355 --> 00:10:59.324
where you can commit
whatever crimes you want

00:10:59.324 --> 00:11:00.493
in your last month in office.

00:11:00.493 --> 00:11:02.894
It's called the transition,
not the Purge.

00:11:02.894 --> 00:11:04.363
This isn't the last week
of middle school,

00:11:04.363 --> 00:11:05.864
where every teacher
shows a movie

00:11:05.864 --> 00:11:08.333
while they Google
"vacation Caribbean cheap"

00:11:08.333 --> 00:11:11.237
and the French teacher
tells you all the good swears.

00:11:11.237 --> 00:11:12.637
I don't remember
George Washington

00:11:12.637 --> 00:11:14.039
spending his last month
in office

00:11:14.039 --> 00:11:15.640
walking around D.C. with an ax,

00:11:15.640 --> 00:11:17.776
chopping down every damn
cherry tree he could find.

00:11:17.776 --> 00:11:19.545
"It's pie night, bitches!"

00:11:19.545 --> 00:11:21.614
The House impeachment managers
also laid out

00:11:21.614 --> 00:11:24.516
the timeline of events
on January 6th

00:11:24.516 --> 00:11:26.385
and Trump's involvement
in those events

00:11:26.385 --> 00:11:28.187
with truly shocking
video evidence

00:11:28.187 --> 00:11:29.655
that, I have to say,
was compelling,

00:11:29.655 --> 00:11:30.989
just to see it all
laid out again,

00:11:30.989 --> 00:11:33.592
because our memories
are so short now.

00:11:33.592 --> 00:11:35.560
I mean, I don't even remember
who won the Super Bowl.

00:11:35.560 --> 00:11:37.596
Tim Brody?

00:11:37.596 --> 00:11:40.031
Was there a guy named Brunk?

00:11:40.031 --> 00:11:42.168
Like there was a Grunk,
or maybe it was a tree

00:11:42.168 --> 00:11:44.636
[ Laughter ]
who only said, "Grunk"?

00:11:44.636 --> 00:11:45.971
It was a violent insurrection

00:11:45.971 --> 00:11:47.672 line:0%
that injured 140 police officers

00:11:47.672 --> 00:11:49.007 line:0%
and tried
to overthrow democracy.

00:11:49.007 --> 00:11:50.976 line:0%
Congress was there and the rest
of us saw it on TV.

00:11:50.976 --> 00:11:53.779 line:0%
The facts are clear as day,
as Raskin explained.

00:11:53.779 --> 00:11:56.214 line:14%
-Our case is based

00:11:56.214 --> 00:11:59.818 line:14%
on cold, hard facts.

00:11:59.818 --> 00:12:01.987
-That's right, the impeachment
case is built on facts,

00:12:01.987 --> 00:12:04.990
and the defense's case is built
on wishes and dreams

00:12:04.990 --> 00:12:07.593
and Sean Hannity's
fantasy list of witnesses,

00:12:07.593 --> 00:12:10.128
which I'm betting includes
some fictional characters, too.

00:12:10.128 --> 00:12:11.329
[ As Hannity ]
I want to call Chuck Schumer,

00:12:11.329 --> 00:12:13.232
Nancy Pelosi, Cory Booker,

00:12:13.232 --> 00:12:15.133
Wanda Maximoff, the Mandalorian,

00:12:15.133 --> 00:12:17.736
and the Doof Warrior.
I want to know what he doofed

00:12:17.736 --> 00:12:18.903
and when he doofed it.

00:12:18.903 --> 00:12:20.038
We all saw what happened.

00:12:20.038 --> 00:12:21.473
It's plain to anyone
who cares to see it.

00:12:21.473 --> 00:12:23.475
The president's supporters
stormed the Capitol

00:12:23.475 --> 00:12:25.945
after he spent months
feeding them unhinged lies

00:12:25.945 --> 00:12:27.779
about the election
being stolen from them,

00:12:27.779 --> 00:12:30.316
culminating in a speech
in which he directed them

00:12:30.316 --> 00:12:33.152
to fight and show strength
by marching down to the Capitol

00:12:33.152 --> 00:12:36.087
and interfering in the lawful
counting of electoral votes,

00:12:36.087 --> 00:12:39.091
all while he watched
and cheered them on.

00:12:39.091 --> 00:12:40.926
At this point, we have
to conclude simply that,

00:12:40.926 --> 00:12:43.595
if Republicans won't hold Trump
accountable for doing that,

00:12:43.595 --> 00:12:45.530
then they support it and,

00:12:45.530 --> 00:12:47.232
if given the chance,
they'll do it again.

00:12:47.232 --> 00:12:49.068
Impeachment should be
the bare minimum

00:12:49.068 --> 00:12:50.736
for inciting a violent sedition.

00:12:50.736 --> 00:12:51.970
If you ask me,
Trump should be...

00:12:51.970 --> 00:12:55.641 line:8%
-Washing his hair
with his dog's shampoo.

00:12:55.641 --> 00:12:57.342
-This has been
"A Closer Look."

